      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"Resting where the sand has washed away\"... that's a very peaceful image, I suppose. But it also sounds quite final. It's as if you're suggesting that the most dignified thing a person can do when they've reached their limit is to just stop. To stop struggling, to stop being, and to just become part of that stillness. Is that what you mean? That there's a certain grace in just letting go?",
